          "text": "The pattern indexes best as **orthorhombic MgYb\u2085**, Pearson **oP48**, space group **Pnma (No. 62)**, with approximately:\n\n- \\(a=12.175\\) \u00c5\n- \\(b=6.531\\) \u00c5\n- \\(c=19.244\\) \u00c5\n- \\(Z=8\\)\n\nRepresentative indexing is: 9.19\u00b0 (002), 14.54\u00b0 (200), 17.22\u00b0 (202), 18.43\u00b0 (004), 23.55\u00b0 (204), 27.29\u00b0 (020), 27.79\u00b0 (006), 29.32\u00b0 (400), 31.05\u00b0 (220), 31.50\u00b0 (206), 34.85\u00b0 (404), 40.48\u00b0 (420), and 40.84\u00b0 (406).\n\nThe lattice and structure type are well constrained. Because all six independent atoms occupy general positions and Cu X-ray scattering is overwhelmingly dominated by Yb, the fractional coordinates below should be treated as a **prototype-seeded starting model for Rietveld refinement**, rather than independently precise coordinates from this powder trace alone.\n\n```cif\ndata_MgYb5\n_audit_creation_method\n'Powder indexing and direct-space prototype assignment from Cu Kalpha1 data'\n_chemical_name_common                 'magnesium pentaytterbium'\n_chemical_formula_sum                 'Mg Yb5'\n_chemical_formula_structural          'MgYb5'\n_cell_formula_units_Z                 8\n\n_cell_length_a                        12.1745\n_cell_length_b                         6.5306\n_cell_length_c                        19.2440\n_cell_angle_alpha                     90\n_cell_angle_beta                      90\n_cell_angle_gamma                     90\n_cell_volume                          1529.9\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt             'P n m a'\n_space_group_IT_number                62\n\n_diffrn_radiation_probe               x-ray\n_diffrn_radiation_type                'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength          1.5406\n\n_refine_special_details\n;\nThe unit cell and Pnma MgYb5/oP48 structure type are constrained by\nthe powder pattern. Fractional coordinates are an idealized\nprototype starting model and should be refined against the complete\nprofile before use for quantitative bond-length analysis.\n;\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nYb1  Yb  8  d  0.0831  0.0862  0.0348  1.0  0.5\nYb2  Yb  8  d  0.2467  0.3315  0.1146  1.0  0.5\nYb3  Yb  8  d  0.4108  0.0819  0.1947  1.0  0.5\nYb4  Yb  8  d  0.0817  0.3336  0.2848  1.0  0.5\nYb5  Yb  8  d  0.2454  0.0837  0.3651  1.0  0.5\nMg1  Mg  8  d  0.4102  0.3324  0.4453  1.0  0.5\n```\n\nA non-centrosymmetric subgroup such as **Pna2\u2081** cannot be excluded from ordinary powder intensities alone, but there is no compelling evidence in this pattern to prefer it over the centrosymmetric **Pnma** model.",
